From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:02:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: isp: offer 1080p60 by default on T8132

The IMX958's config 7 streams the wide view's window at 60 frames per
second. A hold on the J604 listed 60 for 1920x1080, 1280x720 and
640x480 only, delivered them at 60 from the buffer timestamps and the
other sizes at 30 as before, with no new ISP error. Offer it by
default; fps60=N lists 30 at most, as macOS does.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam.c
index fe6273d9a1..79eb464a53 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam.c
@@ -929,13 +929,13 @@ static bool isp_cut_wide(const struct isp_preset *preset,
  *
  * With fps60, the sizes of up to 1920x1080 that the wide view's window can
  * serve are also offered at 60 frames per second, cut from config 7 with
- * the same window, and the stream sends config 7's limit instead. Off by
- * default: no other system streams this mode yet.
+ * the same window, and the stream sends config 7's limit instead. On by
+ * default; fps60=N lists 30 at most, as macOS.
  */
-static bool fps60;
+static bool fps60 = true;
 module_param(fps60, bool, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(fps60,
-		 "T8132: offer 1920x1080, 1280x720 and 640x480 at 60 fps, from the sensor's 60 fps mode (default: off)");
+		 "T8132: offer 1920x1080, 1280x720 and 640x480 at 60 fps, from the sensor's 60 fps mode (default: on)");
 
 #define ISP_FRAME_RATE_FAST 60
 
-- 
2.43.0

